  "solution": {
    "approach": "Count the frequency of each digit from 0 to 9 in the number.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(D)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    char s[1005]; if (scanf(\"%s\", s) != 1) return 0;\n    int counts[10] = {0};\n    for (int i = 0; s[i]; i++) counts[s[i] - '0']++;\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) printf(\"%d : %d\\n\", i, counts[i]);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    string s; if (!(cin >> s)) return 0;\n    vector<int> counts(10, 0);\n    for (char c : s) counts[c - '0']++;\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) cout << i << \" : \" << counts[i] << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNext()) {\n            String s = sc.next();\n            int[] counts = new int[10];\n            for (char c : s.toCharArray()) counts[c - '0']++;\n            for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) System.out.println(i + \" : \" + counts[i]);\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\ndef main():\n    toks = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not toks: return\n    counts = [0] * 10\n    for c in toks[0]: counts[int(c)] += 1\n    for i in range(10): print(f\"{i} : {counts[i]}\")\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require(\"fs\");\nfunction main() {\n    const toks = fs.readFileSync(0, \"utf-8\").trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (!toks || !toks[0]) return;\n    const counts = new Array(10).fill(0);\n    for (const c of toks[0]) counts[parseInt(c, 10)]++;\n    for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) console.log(`${i} : ${counts[i]}`);\n}\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Initialize frequency array of size 10. For each digit in string, increment frequency. Print 'i : count' for i from 0 to 9."
